    {
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Scope, privacy and execution separation",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "All positions and pending orders come from the connected MT5 terminal, including manual and other external trades. **None are certified as this bot’s trades.** Broker account P&L is not strategy-performance evidence. Failed reads retain the last confirmed snapshot: always check freshness. No account number, credentials or trading controls are exposed.\n\nPositions and orders below are from the last successful snapshot; **orange freshness means retained old values, not a fresh reading**. A genuinely empty table is meaningful only when the corresponding count above is zero and freshness is green. SL/TP values of 0 mean unset. Profit/swap use the account currency shown above. All attribution is “not_bot_certified”. A detected account change locks the observer until restart; retained rows still belong to the previously confirmed account.\n\nThis observer uses only MT5 account, position, order and quote read APIs. **Bot execution configuration remains separate**—external positions can exist while the bot is disabled. No history-deal/closed-trade performance is calculated in this first view. Local Prometheus retains observations under the monitoring retention policy; do not expose ports 3000, 9090, 8765 or 8766 remotely. Exporter `/health` means the HTTP process is alive, not that the broker data is fresh."
      },
      "targets": []
    }
